(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m7"] = E["hr-m7"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-7-4"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-7-4-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-7-4","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Formal HR letters","tr":"Resmî İK mektupları","fa":"نامه‌های رسمی منابع انسانی"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can write a formal HR letter: a grievance outcome or a probation review.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda resmî bir İK mektubu yazabileceksin: bir şikâyetin sonucu ya da deneme süresi değerlendirmesi.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یک نامه‌ی رسمی منابع انسانی بنویسی: نتیجه‌ی رسیدگی به یک شکایت یا ارزیابی دوره‌ی آزمایشی."},"hook":{"en":"Put every formal outcome in one clear letter. It shows what was decided, why, and how to appeal. Omar wants to tell Hasan 'it's sorted'. Leyla knows a grievance needs an answer in writing.","tr":"Her resmî sonucu tek ve net bir mektupta yaz. Mektup neye karar verildiğini, nedenini ve nasıl itiraz edileceğini gösterir. Omar, Hasan’a 'hallettik' demek istiyor. Leyla bir şikâyetin yazılı cevap istediğini biliyor.","fa":"هر نتیجه‌ی رسمی را در یک نامه‌ی روشن بنویس. نامه نشان می‌دهد چه تصمیمی گرفته شده، چرا و چطور می‌شود اعتراض کرد. عمر می‌خواهد به حسن بگوید «حل شد». لیلا می‌داند شکایت رسمی جواب کتبی می‌خواهد."},"before":{"en":"Write the core of a formal outcome letter: what you checked, what you decided, what changes and how to appeal.","tr":"Resmî bir sonuç mektubunun özünü yaz: neyi incelediğin, neye karar verdiğin, neyin değiştiği ve nasıl itiraz edileceği.","fa":"هسته‌ی یک نامه‌ی رسمیِ نتیجه را بنویس: چه چیزی را بررسی کردی، چه تصمیمی گرفتی، چه چیزی عوض می‌شود و چطور می‌شود اعتراض کرد."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"One letter that says it all","tr":"Her şeyi söyleyen tek mektup","fa":"نامه‌ای که همه‌چیز را بگوید"},"body":{"en":"A formal letter may be read again later, so it must make sense on its own. Say what you checked and what you decided. Then say what changes and how to appeal.","tr":"Resmî bir mektup sonradan yeniden okunabilir, bu yüzden tek başına anlaşılmalıdır. Neyi incelediğini ve neye karar verdiğini söyle. Sonra neyin değişeceğini ve nasıl itiraz edileceğini yaz.","fa":"نامه‌ی رسمی ممکن است بعدها دوباره خوانده شود، پس باید بدون توضیح اضافه فهمیده شود. بگو چه چیزی را بررسی کردی و چه تصمیمی گرفتی. بعد بگو چه چیزی تغییر می‌کند و چطور می‌شود اعتراض کرد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Formal linking: following, as a result, in addition","tr":"Resmî bağlaçlar: following, as a result, in addition","fa":"ربط‌دهنده‌های رسمی: following، as a result، in addition"},"steps":[{"en":"Open with the event: Following + noun.","tr":"Olayla aç: Following + isim.","fa":"با اتفاق شروع کن: Following و اسم.","ex":"Following our meeting on 3 June, we reviewed the records."},{"en":"Give the result: As a result, + sentence.","tr":"Sonucu ver: As a result, + cümle.","fa":"نتیجه را بگو: As a result، بعد یک جمله.","ex":"As a result, overtime will be offered in turn."},{"en":"Add a second action: In addition, + sentence.","tr":"İkinci bir adım ekle: In addition, + cümle.","fa":"اقدام دوم را اضافه کن: In addition، بعد یک جمله.","ex":"In addition, you will be offered the next two extra shifts."},{"en":"Close with the next step: If you are not satisfied, ...","tr":"Sonraki adımla kapat: If you are not satisfied, ...","fa":"با قدم بعدی تمام کن: If you are not satisfied, ...","ex":"If you are not satisfied, you can appeal within five working days."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Part of the letter","Phrase"],"tr":["Mektubun bölümü","İfade"],"fa":["بخش نامه","عبارت"]},"rows":[["The event","Following our meeting on..."],["What you did","We have reviewed..."],["The outcome","As a result, ..."],["More action","In addition, ..."],["Appeal","If you are not satisfied with this outcome, ..."]]},"tip":{"en":"Following is followed directly by a noun: following our meeting, not following to our meeting.","tr":"Following’den hemen sonra isim gelir: following to our meeting değil, following our meeting.","fa":"بعد از following مستقیم اسم می‌آید: following our meeting، نه following to our meeting."},"wrong":"Following to our meeting, we have reviewed the records.","right":"Following our meeting, we have reviewed the records."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"grievance","meaning":{"en":"A formal complaint by an employee.","tr":"Bir çalışanın resmî şikâyeti.","fa":"شکایت رسمی یک کارمند."}},{"phrase":"We have now completed our review.","meaning":{"en":"Says the checking is finished.","tr":"İncelemenin bittiğini söyler.","fa":"می‌گوید بررسی تمام شده."}},{"phrase":"Your grievance has been partly upheld.","meaning":{"en":"Says the complaint was partly accepted.","tr":"Şikâyetin kısmen kabul edildiğini söyler.","fa":"می‌گوید شکایت تا حدی پذیرفته شده."}},{"phrase":"You can appeal in writing within five working days.","meaning":{"en":"Gives the right to appeal.","tr":"İtiraz hakkını verir.","fa":"حق اعتراض را می‌گوید."}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Every formal outcome goes in writing","tr":"Her resmî sonuç yazılı olur","fa":"هر نتیجه‌ی رسمی کتبی است"},"body":{"en":"The UK Acas Code says a grievance decision should be given in writing without unreasonable delay, and the employee should be told that they can appeal. The time limit for an appeal comes from company policy. A probation review letter has the same shape: the result, the reasons, what happens next. In the UAE, probation can last at most six months.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık’taki Acas Kuralları’na göre şikâyetle ilgili karar gereksiz gecikme olmadan yazılı olarak bildirilmeli ve çalışana itiraz edebileceği söylenmelidir. İtiraz süresini şirket politikası belirler. Deneme süresi değerlendirme mektubu da aynı yapıdadır: sonuç, gerekçeler, sonraki adım. BAE’de deneme süresi en fazla altı ay olabilir.","fa":"طبق آیین‌نامه‌ی Acas در بریتانیا، تصمیم درباره‌ی شکایت باید بدون تأخیر بی‌دلیل و کتبی به کارمند اعلام شود و به او بگویند که می‌تواند اعتراض کند. مهلت اعتراض را آیین‌نامه‌ی شرکت تعیین می‌کند. نامه‌ی ارزیابی دوره‌ی آزمایشی هم همین ساختار را دارد: نتیجه، دلیل‌ها، قدم بعدی. در امارات دوره‌ی آزمایشی حداکثر شش ماه است."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از نامه‌ی مبهم تا نتیجه و راه اعتراض"},"text":"Facts: You reviewed the leave records. Two days will be returned. The person can appeal in writing.","item":"We looked at it. It's sorted now.","why":{"en":"Weak: no reasons, no next step. Strong: review, outcome, appeal.","tr":"Zayıf: neden yok, sonraki adım yok. Güçlü: inceleme, sonuç, itiraz.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول نه دلیل دارد، نه قدم بعدی. نسخه‌ی دوم بررسی، نتیجه و راه اعتراض را می‌گوید."},"answer":"We have reviewed the leave records. As a result, your two days will be returned. You can appeal in writing.","cut":["We looked at it.","It's sorted now."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what a reader could not understand on its own months later.","tr":"Okuyanın aylar sonra tek başına anlayamayacağı sözlere dokun.","fa":"روی حرف‌هایی بزن که خواننده ماه‌ها بعد به‌تنهایی نمی‌فهمدشان."}},"quick":{"prompt":"Under the UK Acas Code, how should a grievance decision be given?","options":["In writing, without unreasonable delay","By phone, so it feels personal","Only if the employee asks"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"In writing, without unreasonable delay, and the employee should be told they can appeal.","tr":"Yazılı olarak ve gereksiz gecikme olmadan; ayrıca çalışana itiraz edebileceği söylenmelidir.","fa":"به‌صورت کتبی و بدون تأخیرِ بی‌دلیل؛ و باید به کارمند گفت که می‌تواند اعتراض کند."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"A decision may be read again months later, and the employee may want to appeal. What form and what timing make that fair?","tr":"Bir karar aylar sonra yeniden okunabilir ve çalışan itiraz etmek isteyebilir. Bunu adil kılan biçim ve zamanlama ne?","fa":"یک تصمیم ممکن است ماه‌ها بعد دوباره خوانده شود و کارمند شاید بخواهد اعتراض کند. چه شکلی و چه زمان‌بندی‌ای این را منصفانه می‌کند؟"}},"remember":{"en":"Event, what you did, outcome, more action, appeal. Result of this lesson: you can write a clear formal outcome. You also have the letter.","tr":"Olay, yaptığın, sonuç, ek adım, itiraz. Bu dersin sonucu: net bir resmî sonuç mektubu yazabilirsin ve elinde mektup olur.","fa":"به همین ترتیب بنویس: اتفاق، کاری که کردی، نتیجه، اقدام بیشتر، اعتراض. حالا می‌توانی نتیجه‌ی رسمی را روشن بنویسی. نامه هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Having reviewed...: one sentence, two steps","tr":"Having reviewed...: tek cümle, iki adım","fa":"Having reviewed...: یک جمله، دو مرحله"},"steps":[{"en":"First step done, then the decision: Having + past participle, + subject + verb.","tr":"Önce biten adım, sonra karar: Having + past participle, + özne + fiil.","fa":"اول کار انجام‌شده را بگو و بعد تصمیم را: Having و اسم مفعول، بعد فاعل و فعل.","ex":"Having reviewed the rota, we agree that it was not fair."},{"en":"The subject must be the one who did the first step.","tr":"Özne, ilk adımı yapanla aynı olmalı.","fa":"فاعل باید همان کسی باشد که مرحله‌ی اول را انجام داده.","ex":"Having spoken to both drivers, I can confirm the dates."},{"en":"Use it once per letter; it sounds formal.","tr":"Mektupta bir kez kullan; resmî duyulur.","fa":"در هر نامه یک بار به کار ببر؛ رسمی به نظر می‌رسد.","ex":"Having considered your appeal, we have decided..."}],"body":{"en":"B2 track: open one paragraph of your letter with Having + past participle.","tr":"B2 yolu: mektubunun bir paragrafını Having + past participle ile aç.","fa":"مسیر B2: یکی از پاراگراف‌های نامه‌ات را با Having و اسم مفعول شروع کن."}},"source":{"en":"Based on the Acas Code of Practice on grievances; probation facts from UAE law.","tr":"Acas’ın şikâyet süreçleriyle ilgili uygulama kurallarına dayanır; deneme süresi bilgileri BAE yasasından alınmıştır.","fa":"بر پایه‌ی آیین‌نامه‌ی Acas درباره‌ی رسیدگی به شکایت؛ اطلاعات دوره‌ی آزمایشی از قانون امارات."}},"story":{"id":"c-hr-7-4-s","course":"hr","unit":"hr-7-4","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","title":{"en":"In Writing","tr":"Yazılı Olarak","fa":"به‌صورت کتبی"},"text":"Hasan had trained half the drivers in Dubai, but he had not had one overtime shift since March. In May he sent Leyla a formal grievance. \"Overtime always goes to the same two people. I would like this investigated.\"\n\nLeyla met him on 3 June and listened. Then she spent two afternoons with the rota. Hasan was right: in April and May, seventy per cent of all overtime had gone to two drivers, both friends of the shift supervisor.\n\nOmar read her summary and sighed. \"Fine. I'll tell Hasan it's sorted.\"\n\n\"He raised a formal grievance,\" Leyla said. \"He gets the answer in writing, with what we found, what will change and how he can appeal.\"\n\nHer letter was short. Following our meeting on 3 June, we have reviewed the overtime records for April and May. Your grievance has been partly upheld. As a result, from 1 July overtime will be offered to all drivers in turn. In addition, you will be offered the next two extra shifts. If you are not satisfied with this outcome, you can appeal in writing within five working days.\n\nHasan read it twice in the canteen. He did not appeal. The next week he asked Leyla, half joking, whether she could write his probation letters for the new trainees too.","vocab":[{"word":"rota","en":"A list of who works which shifts.","tr":"vardiya çizelgesi","fa":"برنامه‌ی شیفت‌ها"},{"word":"uphold","en":"To decide a complaint is right.","tr":"(şikâyeti) haklı bulmak","fa":"(شکایت را) وارد دانستن"},{"word":"appeal","en":"To ask for a decision to be looked at again.","tr":"itiraz etmek","fa":"اعتراض کردن؛ درخواست تجدیدنظر"},{"word":"in turn","en":"One after another, in a fair order.","tr":"sırayla","fa":"به نوبت"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What was Hasan's grievance about?","options":["Overtime always going to the same two drivers","His training hours","A late pay slip"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Which sentence gives the result of the review?","options":["Following our meeting on 3 June, we have reviewed the records.","As a result, from 1 July overtime will be offered to all drivers in turn.","Hasan read it twice."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why does Leyla insist on a letter?","options":["A formal grievance needs a written answer with the right to appeal","Omar cannot write","Hasan asked for a letter"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Why might Hasan not appeal?","options":["The letter was fair, clear and changed something real","He did not read it","The deadline had passed"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Notice the order of Leyla's letter: event, review, outcome, more action, appeal.","tr":"Leyla’nın mektubundaki sıraya dikkat et: olay, inceleme, sonuç, ek adım, itiraz.","fa":"به ترتیب نامه‌ی لیلا دقت کن: اتفاق، بررسی، نتیجه، اقدام بیشتر، اعتراض."},"bridge":{"en":"Next: tell Hasan the outcome face to face, then write the letter.","tr":"Sırada: sonucu Hasan’a yüz yüze söyle, sonra mektubu yaz.","fa":"قدم بعد: نتیجه را رودررو به حسن بگو و بعد نامه را بنویس."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-7-4","course":"hr","unit":"hr-7-4","rounds":[90,60],"topic":{"en":"Giving a Grievance Outcome Face to Face","tr":"Bir Şikâyetin Sonucunu Yüz Yüze Bildirmek","fa":"گفتن نتیجه‌ی شکایت به‌صورت حضوری"},"warmup":{"en":"Have you ever complained about something at work or school? How did you hear the answer?","tr":"Hiç iş yerinde ya da okulda bir şeyden şikâyet ettin mi? Cevabı nasıl öğrendin?","fa":"تا حالا در محل کار یا مدرسه از چیزی شکایت کرده‌ای؟ جوابش را چطور شنیدی؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Thank the person and say what you reviewed.","tr":"Kişiye teşekkür et ve neyi incelediğini söyle.","fa":"از فرد تشکر کن و بگو چه چیزی را بررسی کردی."},{"en":"Give the outcome clearly: upheld, partly upheld or not upheld.","tr":"Sonucu net söyle: kabul edildi, kısmen kabul edildi ya da kabul edilmedi.","fa":"نتیجه را روشن بگو: پذیرفته شد، تا حدی پذیرفته شد یا پذیرفته نشد."},{"en":"Say what will change and when.","tr":"Neyin ve ne zaman değişeceğini söyle.","fa":"بگو چه چیزی و از کی تغییر می‌کند."},{"en":"Explain that a letter will follow and how to appeal.","tr":"Bir mektubun geleceğini ve nasıl itiraz edileceğini açıkla.","fa":"توضیح بده که نامه‌ای می‌آید و چطور می‌شود اعتراض کرد."}],"followups":[{"en":"Say it in 90 seconds, then in 60. Keep the outcome and the appeal.","tr":"Önce 90, sonra 60 saniyede söyle. Sonucu ve itiraz hakkını koru.","fa":"یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه و بعد در ۶۰ ثانیه بگو. نتیجه و حق اعتراض را نگه دار."},{"en":"Now say how someone at your company can raise a formal complaint, step by step.","tr":"Şimdi şirketinde birinin resmî şikâyetini adım adım nasıl iletebileceğini anlat.","fa":"حالا قدم‌به‌قدم بگو در شرکتت یک نفر چطور می‌تواند شکایت رسمی مطرح کند."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"Thank you for raising this.","meaning":{"en":"Respects the complaint.","tr":"Şikâyete saygı gösterir.","fa":"به شکایت احترام می‌گذارد."}},{"phrase":"Your grievance has been partly upheld.","meaning":{"en":"Gives the outcome.","tr":"Sonucu verir.","fa":"نتیجه را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"You'll get this in writing, with how to appeal.","meaning":{"en":"Says what happens next.","tr":"Sonra ne olacağını söyler.","fa":"می‌گوید بعدش چه می‌شود."}}],"culture":{"en":"Tell the person face to face first, then send the letter the same day. Hearing a decision only by email can feel cold; hearing it only in person leaves no record.","tr":"Önce yüz yüze söyle, sonra mektubu aynı gün gönder. Bir kararı yalnızca e-postayla duymak soğuk gelebilir; yalnızca yüz yüze duymak ise kayıt bırakmaz.","fa":"اول رودررو بگو و همان روز نامه را بفرست. شنیدن تصمیم فقط از راه ایمیل ممکن است سرد باشد؛ شنیدنش فقط به‌صورت حضوری هم هیچ سابقه‌ای نمی‌گذارد."},"model":"Hasan, thank you for raising this. Following our meeting on 3 June, we reviewed the overtime records for April and May. Your grievance has been partly upheld. As a result, from 1 July overtime will be offered to all drivers in turn, and you'll get the next two extra shifts. You'll get this in writing today, with how to appeal if you're not satisfied.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I thanked the person and said what I reviewed.","tr":"Kişiye teşekkür ettim ve neyi incelediğimi söyledim.","fa":"از فرد تشکر کردم و گفتم چه چیزی را بررسی کردم."},{"en":"I gave a clear outcome.","tr":"Net bir sonuç verdim.","fa":"نتیجه را روشن گفتم."},{"en":"I said what will change and when.","tr":"Neyin ne zaman değişeceğini söyledim.","fa":"گفتم چه چیزی و کی تغییر می‌کند."},{"en":"I mentioned the letter and the appeal.","tr":"Mektuptan ve itiraz hakkından bahsettim.","fa":"به نامه و حق اعتراض اشاره کردم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-7-4-w","course":"hr","unit":"hr-7-4","type":"writing","title":{"en":"The grievance outcome letter","tr":"Şikâyet sonuç mektubu","fa":"نامه‌ی نتیجه‌ی شکایت"},"difficulty":"hard","prompt":{"en":"Write the outcome letter to Hasan (80-110 words): the meeting, what you reviewed, the outcome, what will change, one more action and how to appeal.","tr":"Hasan’a sonuç mektubunu yaz (80-110 kelime): görüşme, neyi incelediğin, sonuç, neyin değişeceği, ek bir adım ve nasıl itiraz edeceği.","fa":"نامه‌ی نتیجه را برای حسن بنویس (۸۰ تا ۱۱۰ کلمه): جلسه، چیزی که بررسی کردی، نتیجه، چیزی که تغییر می‌کند، یک اقدام دیگر و راه اعتراض."},"model":"Dear Hasan, thank you for raising your concerns about overtime. Following our meeting on 3 June, we have reviewed the overtime records for April and May. We found that most overtime went to two drivers, and your grievance has therefore been partly upheld. As a result, from 1 July overtime will be offered to all drivers in turn. In addition, you will be offered the next two extra shifts. If you are not satisfied with this outcome, you can appeal in writing to Ms Clarke within five working days. Yours sincerely, Leyla Karimi, HR Specialist","frame":"Dear ___, thank you for raising ___. Following our meeting on ___, we have reviewed ___. We found that ___, and your grievance has ___. As a result, ___. In addition, ___. If you are not satisfied with this outcome, you can appeal ___ within ___. Yours sincerely, ___","words":[{"word":"following"},{"word":"as a result"},{"word":"appeal"}],"minWords":80,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: meeting, review, outcome, change, extra action, appeal","Organised: event, review, outcome, action, appeal, in that order","Language: formal linking (following, as a result, in addition)","Tone: formal, fair and clear"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: görüşme, inceleme, sonuç, değişiklik, ek adım, itiraz","Düzen: olay, inceleme, sonuç, adım, itiraz; bu sırayla","Dil: resmî bağlaçlar (following, as a result, in addition)","Üslup: resmî, adil ve net"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: جلسه، بررسی، نتیجه، تغییر، اقدام اضافه، اعتراض","نظم: اتفاق، بررسی، نتیجه، اقدام، اعتراض؛ به همین ترتیب","زبان: ربط‌دهنده‌های رسمی (following، as a result، in addition)","لحن: رسمی، منصفانه و روشن"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"The meeting","tr":"Görüşme","fa":"جلسه"},"find":["following our meeting","following","meeting on"],"sample":"the meeting on 3 June"},{"t":{"en":"What you reviewed","tr":"İncelediğin şey","fa":"چیزی که بررسی کردی"},"find":["we have reviewed","reviewed"],"sample":"the overtime records for April and May"},{"t":{"en":"The outcome","tr":"Sonuç","fa":"نتیجه"},"find":["upheld","we found"],"sample":"partly upheld: most overtime went to two drivers"},{"t":{"en":"What will change","tr":"Ne değişecek","fa":"چه چیزی عوض می‌شود"},"find":["as a result","in addition"],"sample":"overtime offered to all in turn; the next two extra shifts for Hasan"},{"t":{"en":"How to appeal","tr":"Nasıl itiraz edileceği","fa":"چطور اعتراض کند"},"find":["appeal"],"sample":"in writing to Ms Clarke within five working days"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-7-4-p","course":"hr","unit":"hr-7-4","type":"perspective","title":{"en":"Through Hasan's eyes","tr":"Hasan’ın gözünden","fa":"از نگاه حسن"},"minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Hasan. You have just read the outcome letter in the canteen. Write 2 sentences in first person: what part of the letter matters most to you, and why did you decide not to appeal?","tr":"Sen Hasan’sın. Sonuç mektubunu kantinde az önce okudun. Birinci tekil şahısla 2 cümle yaz: mektubun hangi kısmı senin için en önemli ve neden itiraz etmemeye karar verdin?","fa":"تو حسن هستی و همین حالا نامه‌ی نتیجه را در سلف خوانده‌ای. از زبان خودت دو جمله بنویس: کدام بخش نامه برایت مهم‌تر است و چرا تصمیم گرفتی اعتراض نکنی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-7-4-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-7-4","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-7-4","kind":"blank","point":2,"prompt":"___ our call on Monday, I am writing to confirm your start date.","options":["Following","Following to","After of"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Following: 'Following our call' means after it, in formal letters. 'Following to' and 'After of' add a wrong preposition.","tr":"Following: resmî yazılarda 'Following our call' görüşmemizden sonra demektir. 'Following to' ve 'After of' yanlış bir edat ekler.","fa":"Following درست است، چون در نامه‌ی رسمی Following our call یعنی بعد از تماس‌مان. following to و after of حرف اضافه‌ی غلط دارند."},"hint2":{"en":"The gap opens with the event, and a noun follows (our call). Which formal word works on its own before a noun?","tr":"Boşluk olayla açılıyor ve ardından bir isim geliyor (our call). Hangi resmî kelime bir isimden önce tek başına kullanılır?","fa":"جای خالی با رویداد شروع می‌شود و بعدش یک اسم آمده (⁨our call⁩). کدام کلمه‌ی رسمی به‌تنهایی قبل از اسم می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-7-4","kind":"blank","point":2,"prompt":"The rota was not fair. ___, it will be changed from 1 July.","options":["As a result","Although","In spite of"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"As a result: it links a cause to its effect, and a comma follows. 'Although' and 'In spite of' show contrast, not a result.","tr":"As a result: bir nedeni sonucuna bağlar ve ardından virgül gelir. 'Although' ve 'In spite of' sonucu değil, karşıtlığı gösterir.","fa":"As a result درست است، چون علت را به نتیجه وصل می‌کند و بعدش ویرگول می‌آید. although و in spite of تقابل را نشان می‌دهند، نه نتیجه را."},"hint2":{"en":"The second sentence is the result of the first. Which linker says that?","tr":"İkinci cümle birincinin sonucu. Bunu hangi bağlaç söyler?","fa":"جمله‌ی دوم نتیجه‌ی جمله‌ی اول است. کدام حرف ربط همین را می‌گوید؟"}},{"from":"hr-7-4","kind":"mcq","point":1,"prompt":"Which line should a formal grievance outcome letter include?","options":["How the employee can appeal","A joke to keep it friendly","The names of other employees who complained"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"How the employee can appeal: a formal outcome letter must tell them their next right. A joke is out of place, and other employees' names break their privacy.","tr":"Çalışanın nasıl itiraz edebileceği: resmî sonuç yazısı ona bir sonraki hakkını söylemelidir. Şaka yersizdir; diğer çalışanların adları onların gizliliğini bozar.","fa":"راه اعتراض کارمند؛ نامه‌ی رسمی نتیجه باید حق بعدی‌اش را بگوید. شوخی جایش نیست و اسم کارمندان دیگر حریم خصوصی آن‌ها را می‌شکند."}},{"from":"hr-7-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"She ___ off twice since March.","options":["has been","was","is"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has been: 'since March' runs until now, so the present perfect. 'Was' is for finished time, and 'is' doesn't go with since.","tr":"has been: 'since March' bugüne kadar sürer, bu yüzden present perfect. 'Was' bitmiş zaman içindir; 'is' since ile kullanılmaz.","fa":"has been درست است، چون since March تا الان ادامه دارد و حال کامل می‌خواهد. was برای زمان تمام‌شده است و is با since نمی‌آید."},"hint2":{"en":"since March shows a pattern that runs up to now. Which tense joins the past to now?","tr":"since March şimdiye kadar süren bir örüntüyü gösterir. Geçmişi şimdiye hangi zaman bağlar?","fa":"⁨since March⁩ الگویی را نشان می‌دهد که تا الان ادامه دارد. کدام زمان گذشته را به حالا وصل می‌کند؟"}},{"from":"hr-7-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Your medical form ___ last week.","options":["was received","received","is receive"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"was received: the form received the action last week, so was + past participle. 'Received' alone says the form received something, and 'is receive' is not English.","tr":"was received: form geçen hafta eylemi aldı, bu yüzden was + üçüncü hâl. Tek başına 'received' formun bir şey aldığını söyler; 'is receive' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"was received درست است، چون فرم هفته‌ی پیش دریافت شد و was و اسم مفعول لازم است. received تنها یعنی خود فرم چیزی گرفته و is receive انگلیسی نیست."}},{"from":"hr-4-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"What should you do BEFORE replying to a complaint?","options":["Explain the budget","Summarise the feelings and reasons you heard","Promise a solution"],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"Summarise the feelings and reasons you heard: the person knows you listened. The budget or a quick promise comes too early.","tr":"Duyduğun duyguları ve nedenleri özetle: kişi dinlendiğini anlar. Bütçe ya da hızlı bir söz çok erken gelir.","fa":"حس‌ها و دلیل‌هایی را که شنیدی خلاصه کن تا طرف بفهمد گوش داده‌ای. حرف از بودجه یا قول سریع خیلی زود است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
